Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Prometheus Cannot Scrape Jenkins
Symptoms: Jenkins target shows as DOWN in Prometheus

Solutions:

Verify Jenkins Prometheus plugin is installed and configured
Check Jenkins is accessible at http://localhost:8080/prometheus
Restart Jenkins service: sudo systemctl restart jenkins
Issue 2: Alerts Not Firing
Symptoms: Expected alerts don't appear in Prometheus

Solutions:

Check alert rule syntax: /usr/local/bin/promtool check rules /etc/prometheus/jenkins_rules.yml
Verify Prometheus configuration: /usr/local/bin/promtool check config /etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml
Check Prometheus logs: sudo journalctl -u prometheus -f
Issue 3: Webhook Not Receiving Alerts
Symptoms: Alertmanager shows alerts but webhook doesn't receive them

Solutions:

Verify webhook server is running: ps aux | grep webhook_receiver
Check Alertmanager configuration and restart: sudo systemctl restart alertmanager
Test webhook manually: curl -X POST http://localhost:5001/webhook -d '{"test": "data"}'
Issue 4: High Memory Usage
Symptoms: System becomes slow or unresponsive

Solutions:

Reduce Prometheus retention: Add --storage.tsdb.retention.time=7d to Prometheus service
Increase scrape intervals in prometheus.yml
Monitor system resources: htop or free -h
